---
title: Grilled Tandoori Chicken Skewers
servings: 6
cuisine: indian
main_protein: chicken
prep_time: "140 minutes"
cook_time: "10 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
leftover_portions: 2
prep:
  - Mince 3 garlic cloves and 1 tablespoon fresh ginger
  - Cut chicken thighs into 2-inch pieces
  - Soak wooden skewers in water for 10-15 minutes
  - Mince cucumber, parsley and mint for the tzatziki
---

= Tandoori Chicken

In a #large bowl{}, whisk @plain yogurt{1%cup}, @garlic{2%cloves}, minced, @fresh ginger{1%tablespoon}, minced, all the spices (@smoked paprika{1%teaspoon}, @ground coriander{1%teaspoon}, @ground cumin{1%teaspoon}, @ground turmeric{1%teaspoon}, @ground cloves{0.5%teaspoon}, @cayenne pepper{0.5%teaspoon}) and season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste. Place @boneless skinless chicken thighs{2%lbs}, cut into 2-in pieces, in marinade and toss until they're evenly submerged in the marinade. Cover with plastic wrap and marinade chicken in fridge at least ~{2%hours} or overnight.

Once chicken is done marinating, remove from marinade and pat dry. Discard marinade. Thread chicken onto #wooden skewers{}. (For best results, soak skewers in water 10-15 minutes to prevent them from breaking while grilling.)

Grill tandoori chicken on a #grill{} over medium-high heat ~{4%minutes} on each side, turning occasionally until chicken registers 165F, about 8-10 minutes of cook time total. Keep chicken warm. Alternatively if you don't have access to a grill: in a #large skillet{}, pan sear the skewers in 1-2 tablespoons vegetable oil, turning occasionally until chicken is browned and registers 165F.

= Tzatziki Sauce

In a #small bowl{}, whisk all sauce ingredients (@plain yogurt{1.5%cups}, @cucumber{0.5%cup}, minced, @lemon juice{2%tablespoons}, @garlic{1%clove}, minced, @fresh parsley{2%tablespoons}, minced, @fresh mint{2%tablespoons}, minced) until smooth. Season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} to taste. Refrigerate until ready to use.

Serve tandoori chicken skewers hot with tzatziki sauce. Enjoy!
